# Quantitative rational linear algebra

This file was automatically generated by Codex.

This module proves uniform height and Euclidean operator-norm estimates for
rational matrices, nonsingular inverses, pivot right inverses on their ranges,
and orthogonal projections and their complements. It also counts matrices of
bounded height and selects bounded-height bases without a spanning-list cost.
The proof clears denominators and uses determinant and adjugate formulas.
All statements and supporting definitions use only Mathlib and this module.

Source: `blueprint/formalization_blueprint.tex`, `lem:rational-linear`,
lines 416–420. Verified library references are
`Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas` (reduced numerator and denominator),
`Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Adjugate` (Cramer's rule),
`Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank` (row and column rank), and
`Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Projection.Basic` (orthogonal projection).
The rational height convention agrees with `Rat.mulHeight₁_eq_max` in
`Mathlib.NumberTheory.Height.NumberField`.
The bounded-height frequency development uses the same independent
denominator and determinant machinery (`lem:height`, lines 603–619).
